title Caravan cohort -- the widest set a document may run is derived, never chosen
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, Standfast on reds first, one council-rota doc deep-read, condense REMEMBER, send the finished increment.
think Standfast first. The living REDS rows read 80, 83, 84, 85 with prose notes 81, 82, 86, 87 and the reopened 85. Every one carries a closure line and a witness on metal -- 84 closed on measurement 20260819.145920, 85 reopened and closed 20260819.134229 with the witness_claim_check loom standing, 83's prevention landed as living_card_ascii_witness. No open agent-closable red stands, so the constructive queue opens honestly rather than by skipping the corrective one.
think Council rota by lap index -- 465 .kyri logs on disk, this is lap 466, and 466 mod 27 = 7, so the deep-read was foundations/20260813-142420_mycelium-the-consensus-protocol.md. Its one law beneath ninety-eight modules governed this rung directly: the order is decided once, by everyone, and read by everyone the same way. A cohort derived by exhaustive ascending search over subsets is exactly that shape -- a pure function of the declaration's bytes, so two supervisors reading one document derive one cohort without ever speaking. Nothing here is arbitrated.
think The crux was already named by the last lap's recommend and by REMEMBER's live edge: a shape with room for three at once, and whether a supervisor derives the widest set it may run rather than the widest pair. The first move was arithmetic rather than code. A ring's widest set is floor(n/2), so a non-adjacent triple wants a ring of six -- and capabilities.max_children is 4, so a ring of six is past what one supervisor's table holds. Raising that bound to reach for a hex ring would have been the wrong lap; the honest reading is that a ring simply has no room for three, and the shape that does is one this tree already knows.
think That shape is a server and its clients. serve.rye had already proved two clients never hear each other's bell -- proved it as a refusal, an absence of traffic made checkable. This rung adds the third client and turns that same isolation into room a supervisor can spend. serial_three_clients.bron gives each client an ask region it writes, a back region the virtualiser writes, and a taken tail it holds alone; no region and no channel joins any client to any other, and the virtualiser touches every one of them.
think The counterexample fell out of the shape rather than being contrived for it, which is what makes it worth keeping. The virtualiser is declared first, so a supervisor taking each domain in declaration order that still fits takes the virtualiser and runs one child, where the widest set runs three. The first fit is never unsafe -- it always answers a set that may genuinely run together -- it is simply threefold narrow on the plainest shape in the tree. That is why the derivation is exhaustive, and the greedy reading stays in the module as a named control so the claim is proven against it rather than asserted.
think A set may run together exactly when every pair in it may, because both hazards are relations between exactly two domains. So concurrent.rye's judge_pair is reused whole rather than restated one size up, and conflict_in walks pairs and names the first offender by domain and by which hazard refused it.
think The cost of exhaustive is named rather than hidden. Weighing every subset is 2^n, bounded above by max_subsets = 1 << channels.max_domains = 256, so the search is bounded by the same constant that bounds the roster. A supervisor bounds its roster; it never bounds its search and then calls the narrower answer the widest. widest_cohort carries the true count out through weighed_out so the run prints what the search actually spent -- 16 subsets for these four-domain documents -- rather than the ceiling.
think One honest cost surfaced only by running it. The taken tail is held by its client alone, so it carries no direction at all -- one writer, no reader -- and shape_of answers no directed flow to derive rather than naming a ring. That reads oddly until it is stated plainly, and then it is exactly right: a region only one domain can reach is memory rather than a wire, and the room this shape has comes from precisely that privacy. Named in the declaration comment, in the module prose, in the README, and asserted in the witness, the same way the mute document's shape cost was.
think The reaping rule gained a third edge. inflight.rye learned it with one child standing, concurrent.rye with two, and here with three: reporting the first outcome the instant it arrives strands a pair rather than a single sibling. The loose reading is carried as a named control and measured -- unreaped_at_report 2, reaped_late 2 -- against the safe reading's 0 and 0.
obs Building the ring of six was the tempting lap and the wrong one. The bound that stopped it (max_children 4) is not an obstacle to route around; it is the reading that a ring cannot offer a triple within one supervisor's table, and following the arithmetic instead of the bound found the far better shape.
obs The greedy control is the whole justification for the exhaustive search's cost. Without a document where first-fit is measurably narrower, an exhaustive derivation is expense with no evidence -- so the counterexample and the search landed in the same round rather than the search alone.
obs Both new claims are order-independent in the witness, since three children printing at the same moment interleave differently run to run. Every check reads the selftest output natively with contains, never a shell grep over interpolated output (REDS #76 / #85).
loom witness=caravan_cohort_witness subsets_weighed=16 widest=3 first_fit=1 children=9 stages=5 cohort_stages=2 peak_in_flight=3 reaped=9 unreaped_at_report=0 asks_home=6
file caravan/systems/serial_three_clients.bron one server and three clients -- the first shape in the arc with room for three at once, its private-tail shape cost stated
file caravan/cohort.rye the widest set derived by weighing every subset, the greedy reading kept as a named control, and a stage of three reaped whole before any verdict
file tools/caravan_cohort_witness.rish GREEN on metal -- the room a ring lacks, the widest against the first fit, the lap, the refusal, and the reaping
file caravan/README.md the ladder row and the section that reads why the widest set is derived rather than chosen
file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge moved to the cohort finding; the concurrent edge condensed into the prior-edges line
recommend keep-going the rolling cohort -- whether a supervisor may hold the widest set and refill a slot as each child finishes, rather than reaping the whole stage before the next begins, so the safe-reaping rule and the room both hold at once
